test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T21:47:01.0540023Z             "body": "This draft preserves original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging and lifecycle controls. Publishing remains disabled; release acceptance is blocked.\n\nCandidate 953ba87 preserves failed SDK, actual Codex and process-hint control workspaces, retains original and cleanup errors together, and adds bounded diagnostic receipts. Actual SDK/Codex baseline controls reproduced discarded errors and evidence; fixed negative and healthy controls pass on supported Node22/24. All five original group-hint tests pass in real fresh Linux PID namespaces on Node20/22/24; the whole host exceeds the unchanged snapshot row cap. This does not establish the native macOS failure cause. Healthy actual Codex1000 steps passes locally in36.210s with modelTurns0/owned0. Fresh Node22 production install/all runtime smokes, typecheck and lint pass;297-file dry pack excludes tests/evidence.\n\nBrowser core remains reviewed9f9750ae24604e2099e1c1f6564d5d6cb3d19d30dfbc8b5ec61ba18c0989e25a: VP9 metadata, one exact capture-unavailable retry under the original deadline, and ordered existing viewport commands. A stronger actual first-JPEG regression fails the unmodified3eb baseline and passes on20/22/24. An experimental hidden-window change failed and was rejected; no frame skip/seek/warmup, encoder rewrite, input replay, default channel/transport change or raised limits.\n\nLatest completed native96 atcc9562b: batch39842071053 reports1634 passes/4 failures; original39842070912 reports601/7; completed test summaries2235/11. Separately, Windows actual Codex fails CRASHED at75 durable reported steps, no result, operatorAttentionRequiredtrue, recovered_interrupted; guardian read journal_unavailable, exit1, journal progress rpc_timeout. Effects beyond75 and worker/browser exits remain unknown. Linux/Mac actual Codex1000 pass36.057s/87.985s, model0/owned0. All five installed-package steps, all component lanes and12 actual schema races pass. All17 job logs resolved; one partial EOF read retained with successful ordinary retry.\n\nBatch Linux209/213/213 pass; Mac210/3 fails SDK986, sync997 and group-hint orphan control; Windows204/1 fails Firefox403 overall timeout despite typed403/zero completed/one request and response. Mac raw1000 and separate server/direct-pipe1000 pass. Four separate Windows Firefox controls each pass10 fresh/230 actions; they do not waive main failures. Windows SDK startup control fails init after1/2 fulfilled probes; separate traced storage success does not rule out IO/ACL issues.\n\nOriginal Linux200/0 Mac198/2 Windows197/3 include8 additive stock references each. PNG12/12, PCM11/12; Windows WebKit stays ready0 and original PCM/VP9 fail. Mac gray recording and Firefox trusted-click interruption after73 confirmed clicks remain. Windows legacy2/1 includes headed fresh3 at7/23; Mac fresh video2/1; Docker2/0.\n\nNative96 retains117 actual JPEG headers:101 at320x240 and16 at320x98 across two Chromium main/fresh streams including frame1. Gray padding explains y100/y239 in browser and independent ffmpeg frame zero despite red source PNG. Ordered viewport setup did not eliminate native clipping. Controlled real Chromium experiments demonstrate the clipping mechanism, not a complete native fix.\n\nFull process rows retained: Windows privacy scoped0/legacyOnly4 and pair10 scoped0/legacyOnly2 are separate snapshots, not clearance of prior survivors. No role/name/age/window filtering, hint-authorized signals or retrospective clearance of native94/native89/historical136/142 gaps. Native97 runs39853792171/39853792190 are active. Full evidence and limitations: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md and docs/evidence/native96-summary.json. G18 BLOCKED; no merge/publication.",
